epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/06-live-reconciliation-and-degradation/verification-bundle.md:27:- canonical archive derivation\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/05-package-export.md:5:Export the currently reviewed package as a bounded `.mpkz` archive with an `_nav.md` manifest, while keeping the review workspace open when export fails or a prior download URL expires.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/05-package-export.md:14:- **Key Constraint:** The review surface must stay process-aware and version-aware without turning into a generic document-management product, archive browser, or broader publication workflow in the same epic.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/05-package-export.md:18:Deliver the package-export pipeline for reviewed package snapshots so the user can request a bounded archive from the same workspace. Export remains a two-phase flow in this story: POST returns signed metadata, then GET streams the archive. Until a downstream process-module epic publishes package snapshots in normal product flow, this story is exercised through tests and manual Convex seeding.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/05-package-export.md:26:- Return a bounded `.mpkz` archive for the currently reviewed package snapshot\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/05-package-export.md:42:- Liminal Build markdown package library for `.mpk` and `.mpkz` archive handling\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/05-package-export.md:85:This story adds export preflight, signed download metadata, and archive streaming for the currently reviewed package snapshot.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/05-package-export.md:92:| Download package export | `GET` | `/api/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}/review/exports/{exportId}` | Phase 2 of export. Consumes the signed token issued by the POST, re-verifies access and exportability, and streams the `.mpkz` archive as `application/gzip`. Returns `404 REVIEW_TARGET_NOT_FOUND` when the token is expired, tampered, or missing |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/05-package-export.md:114:The first-cut export format is a Liminal Build markdown package (`.mpkz`): a gzip-wrapped tar archive containing one file per package member alongside an `_nav.md` manifest. The manifest is itself a reviewable markdown document that records the package identity, package-level metadata, and the included artifact version identities in a navigation tree. An uncompressed `.mpk` variant exists in the underlying format but is not emitted by first-cut web export.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/05-package-export.md:142:- Export preflight returns bounded signed-download metadata and the resulting archive name ends in `.mpkz`\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/05-package-export.md:143:- The exported archive matches the reviewed package snapshot and includes an `_nav.md` manifest with package and artifact version identities, even when the snapshot spans multiple producing processes\\n./tests/integration/review-workspace.test.ts:571:        processHistoryItems: [],\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/02-artifact-versions-and-revision-review.md:14:- **Key Constraint:** The review surface must stay process-aware and version-aware without turning into a generic document-management product, archive browser, or broader publication workflow in the same epic.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/stories/00-foundation.md:34:- Full markdown review, export, or archive derivation behavior\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/06-reopen-unavailable-and-degraded-review-states.md:14:- **Key Constraint:** The review surface must stay process-aware and version-aware without turning into a generic document-management product, archive browser, or broader publication workflow in the same epic.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/06-reopen-unavailable-and-degraded-review-states.md:33:- Global archive browsing or broader review-library behavior\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/01-process-entry-and-bootstrap/verification-bundle.md:61:- `convex/processHistoryItems.ts`\\n./tests/integration/process-work-surface.test.ts:190:    processHistoryItemsByProcessId: {\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:73:The platform's longest-standing constraint is that the process work surface is process-aware, not a generic document browser. Review has to inherit that stance. Users enter review from the process they are working on, with that process context carried forward. The review workspace is not a cross-project artifact library, not a global archive, and not a substitute for source-management workflows — all of those are explicitly deferred. What review is, in Epic 4, is a dedicated surface that opens one artifact or one durable output package, preserves markdown structure and Mermaid diagrams in place, surfaces version history on one artifact, and exports a bounded package for users who need the outputs outside the platform.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:152:| Use generic `archiver` / `jszip` for export | Rejected | Bypasses the MDV-derived format that is the intended Liminal Build package primitive |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:289:| Export package action | `POST /api/projects/:projectId/processes/:processId/review/packages/:packageId/export` | Phase 1 of export: returns signed download metadata for a `.mpkz` archive; the subsequent GET to `/review/exports/:exportId` performs the actual byte stream |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:556:- **Exportability tracks durability, not workspace renderability alone**: a package is exportable when it has at least one durable member and no member is unavailable. Members with `status: unsupported` stay exportable because the archive packages pinned bytes, not in-workspace render output.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/tech-design.md:579:| Full archive / turn / chunk browsing | Out of scope | Feature 5 follow-on | Feature 5 epic |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/00-foundation/sonnet-review.json:1:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"result\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"success\\\",\\\"is_error\\\":false,\\\"duration_ms\\\":427594,\\\"duration_api_ms\\\":426924,\\\"num_turns\\\":43,\\\"result\\\":\\\"The file write is pending your approval. Here is the full review:\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## VERDICT: REVISE\\\\n\\\\nOne MAJOR finding must be resolved before this foundation is clean enough to serve as the reference baseline for Stories 1–6.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## STORY0_REQUIREMENTS_MATRIX\\\\n\\\\n| Requirement | Status |\\\\n|---|---|\\\\n| Shared route constants and endpoint vocabulary | SATISFIED |\\\\n| `process.processType`, `.status`, `.availableActions` values | SATISFIED |\\\\n| `history.kind`, `.lifecycleState` values | SATISFIED |\\\\n| `live.messageType`, `.entityType` values | SATISFIED |\\\\n| Shared section error and live update contracts | SATISFIED |\\\\n| `processSurface` state slice in `AppState` | SATISFIED |\\\\n| Route parsing: process route checked before project-shell | SATISFIED |\\\\n| `processSurface.projectId/processId` populated on route parse | SATISFIED |\\\\n| Pure `applyLiveProcessMessage` helper | SATISFIED |\\\\n| WebSocket plugin scaffold | SATISFIED |\\\\n| Process routes scaffold | SATISFIED |\\\\n| `ProcessWorkSurfaceService` interface + NotImplemented stub | SATISFIED |\\\\n| `ProcessModuleRegistry` + functional registry | SATISFIED |\\\\n| `ProcessLiveHub` + `NoopProcessLiveHub` | SATISFIED |\\\\n| `app.ts` plugin/route registration order | SATISFIED |\\\\n| All three new Convex tables with correct fields and indexes | SATISFIED |\\\\n| `currentRequestHistoryItemId` pointer added to `processes` | SATISFIED |\\\\n| New Convex modules are guideline-compliant | SATISFIED |\\\\n| **Modified `convex/processes.ts` normalized to Epic 2 guidelines** | **VIOLATED** |\\\\n| All required fixtures present and valid | SATISFIED |\\\\n| `renderShell` supports non-`/projects` routes | SATISFIED |\\\\n| No Story 1+ user-visible behavior introduced | SATISFIED |\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## TEST_DIFF_AUDIT\\\\n\\\\nZero test file changes from base commit. This is correct — Chunk 0 specifies 0 TC and 0 non-TC tests per the test plan. The exit gate is typecheck + build only.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## BLOCKING_FINDINGS\\\\n\\\\n### F-1 — MAJOR | HIGH confidence\\\\n\\\\n**`convex/processes.ts` was modified in Story 0 but not normalized to Epic 2 Convex guidelines.**\\\\n\\\\nObserved violations in the file as modified:\\\\n\\\\n```ts\\\\n// line 1 — uses generic imports instead of typed\\\\nimport { mutationGeneric as mutation, queryGeneric as query } from 'convex/server';\\\\n\\\\n// lines 37, 64 — ctx: any, args: any\\\\nhandler: async (ctx: any, args: any) => { ... }\\\\n\\\\n// line 40 — unbounded collect\\\\n.order('desc').collect();\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nAdditionally, `convex/schema.ts` shows a duplicate index on the `processes` table:\\\\n\\\\n```ts\\\\n.index('by_projectId_updatedAt', ['projectId', 'updatedAt'])     // old\\\\n.index('by_projectId_and_updatedAt', ['projectId', 'updatedAt']) // new — both index same fields\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nThe tech-design.md Issue table explicitly resolves this: *\\\\\\\"This design standardizes new and modified Convex modules on guideline-compliant validators, typed contexts, bounded queries, and explicit indexes. Existing scaffold shortcuts are treated as implementation debt, not as design precedent.\\\\\\\"* The verification bundle's own orchestrator note flags this as a primary scrutiny point.\\\\n\\\\n**Why this matters:** `processes.ts` is the reference file for later story implementers. Leaving `ctx: any` and `.collect()` in place after modification signals that those patterns are acceptable precedent. Stories 2–6 will replicate the debt.\\\\n\\\\n**Required fix:** Replace `queryGeneric`/`mutationGeneric` with typed imports, replace `ctx: any`/`args: any` with proper context types and explicit validators, replace `.collect()` with `.take(n)`, remove the duplicate `by_projectId_updatedAt` index.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## NONBLOCKING_WARNINGS\\\\n\\\\n**F-2 — MINOR:** `processLiveUnavailableErrorFixture` uses `requestErrorSchema` with `status: 503`. The fixture is type-valid (it fits `live.error`), but naming and the 503 status imply an HTTP response, which contradicts the tech-design resolution that live unavailability is a transport state, not an HTTP error. Renaming and a clarifying comment would prevent Story 6 misuse.\\\\n\\\\n**F-3 — MINOR (covered by F-1):** Duplicate `processes` table indexes.\\\\n\\\\n**F-4 — MINOR:** `bootstrap.ts` `loadParsedRoute` falls through to `getProjectShell` for `process-work-surface` routes. Within Story 0 scope, but Story 1 must add a dedicated branch or it will call the shell API unnecessarily on every process route.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## UNRESOLVED\\\\n\\\\n**U-1:** `ProcessWorkSurfaceModule.buildSurfaceProjection` receives `processId: string` rather than `process: ProcessRecord` as shown in tech-design-server.md. Cannot confirm impact until Stories 2–3 implement the first concrete module.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## GATE_RESULT\\\\n\\\\nClaimed PASS (typecheck + build) per verification bundle. Could not independently verify — the `typecheck` command required approval not granted during this session. Accepted as claimed; gate failure would escalate to BLOCK.\\\",\\\"stop_reason\\\":\\\"end_turn\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"7aebeca1-dc8c-43a0-926a-06ae9502e2c0\\\",\\\"total_cost_usd\\\":1.0892933999999999,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":170,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":91994,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":1330853,\\\"output_tokens\\\":22970,\\\"server_tool_use\\\":{\\\"web_search_requests\\\":0,\\\"web_fetch_requests\\\":0},\\\"service_tier\\\":\\\"standard\\\",\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":91994,\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0},\\\"inference_geo\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"iterations\\\":[{\\\"input_tokens\\\":8,\\\"output_tokens\\\":1464,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":100068,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":4335,\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0,\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":4335},\\\"type\\\":\\\"message\\\"}],\\\"speed\\\":\\\"standard\\\"},\\\"modelUsage\\\":{\\\"claude-sonnet-4-6\\\":{\\\"inputTokens\\\":170,\\\"outputTokens\\\":22970,\\\"cacheReadInputTokens\\\":1330853,\\\"cacheCreationInputTokens\\\":91994,\\\"webSearchRequests\\\":0,\\\"costUSD\\\":1.0892933999999999,\\\"contextWindow\\\":200000,\\\"maxOutputTokens\\\":32000}},\\\"permission_denials\\\":[{\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Bash\\\",\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_01UD9rnr5wb9PmL71CW5ZdeK\\\",\\\"tool_input\\\":{\\\"command\\\":\\\"corepack pnpm run typecheck 2>&1 | tail -30\\\",\\\"timeout\\\":60000,\\\"description\\\":\\\"Run typecheck gate\\\"}},{\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Bash\\\",\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_01UwejwDC59cmMy1kBRF5S1p\\\",\\\"tool_input\\\":{\\\"command\\\":\\\"corepack pnpm run typecheck\\\",\\\"timeout\\\":60000,\\\"description\\\":\\\"Run typecheck gate\\\"}},{\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Write\\\",\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_01CAdP2WqUxx26SJNAkuJizw\\\",\\\"tool_input\\\":{\\\"file_path\\\":\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/00-foundation/sonnet-review.md\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"# Story 0 Foundation — Compliance Review\\\\n\\\\n**Reviewer:** Claude Sonnet 4.6  \\\\n**Date:** 2026-04-14  \\\\n**Story base commit:** `c9a63ef2b71e7bdfa380a6c7313f3a2b38e7c9ac`  \\\\n**Verification bundle:** `story-verification/00-foundation/verification-bundle.md`\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## VERDICT: REVISE\\\\n\\\\nOne MAJOR finding (Convex normalization) must be resolved before the foundation\\\\nis clean enough to be the reference baseline for Stories 1–6. The issue is a\\\\nconfirmed scope omission, not speculative. Everything else is PASS or MINOR.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## STORY0_REQUIREMENTS_MATRIX\\\\n\\\\n| Requirement | Status | Notes |\\\\n|---|---|---|\\\\n| Shared route constant `/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}` | SATISFIED | `processWorkSurfaceRouteTemplate` and companion patterns defined in `process-work-surface.ts` |\\\\n| Shared endpoint vocabulary (bootstrap, start, resume, respond, live WS) | SATISFIED | All six path patterns defined and exported; path-builder helpers present |\\\\n| `process.processType` values | SATISFIED | `ProductDefinition`, `FeatureSpecification`, `FeatureImplementation` |\\\\n| `process.status` values | SATISFIED | All 7 values in `processStatusSchema` and mirrored in Convex validator |\\\\n| `process.availableActions` values (`start`, `respond`, `resume`, `review`, `restart`) | SATISFIED | `processSurfaceAvailableActionSchema` in `process-work-surface.ts` |\\\\n| `history.kind` values | SATISFIED | All 6 kinds in `processHistoryItemKindSchema` |\\\\n| `history.lifecycleState` values | SATISFIED | `current`, `finalized` |\\\\n| `live.messageType` values | SATISFIED | `snapshot`, `upsert`, `complete`, `error` |\\\\n| `live.entityType` values | SATISFIED | All 5 entity types |\\\\n| Shared section error contract (code, message) | SATISFIED | `processSurfaceSectionErrorSchema` with typed code enum |\\\\n| Shared live update contract (all 9 fields per spec) | SATISFIED | `liveProcessMessageBaseSchema` covers all fields; discriminated union covers all entity types |\\\\n| `processSurface` state slice in `AppState` | SATISFIED | `processSurfaceStateSchema` in `state.ts`; `processSurface` key in `appStateSchema`; default values in `defaultAppState` |\\\\n| Route parsing: process route matched before project-shell pattern | SATISFIED | `processMatch` check precedes `projectMatch` in `parseRoute()` |\\\\n| `processId` and `projectId` populated in `processSurface` slice on route parse | SATISFIED | `getProcessSurfaceRouteIdentity` called in `bootstrap.ts`; identity fields stored in `processSurface` initial state |\\\\n| Pure `applyLiveProcessMessage` helper | SATISFIED | Implemented in `process-live.ts`; handles all 5 entity types and error messages; stale-message guard present |\\\\n| WebSocket plugin scaffold in server | SATISFIED | `websocket.plugin.ts` registers with Fastify; decorates app with `NoopProcessLiveHub` |\\\\n| Process routes scaffold in server | SATISFIED | `routes/processes.ts` stubs `registerProcessRoutes`; exports route-pattern constants |\\\\n| `ProcessWorkSurfaceService` interface + NotImplemented stub | SATISFIED | `process-work-surface.service.ts`; stub throws `story0NotImplementedErrorCode` |\\\\n| `ProcessModuleRegistry` interface + functional registry | SATISFIED | Registry is functional (register/get/list); throws NotImplemented when no module registered |\\\\n| `ProcessLiveHub` interface + `NoopProcessLiveHub` | SATISFIED | In `process-live-hub.ts`; subscribe and publish both no-ops |\\\\n| `app.ts` registers websocket plugin and process routes in correct order | SATISFIED | `websocketPlugin` registered before `registerProcessRoutes`; `ProcessLiveHub` wired as optional decoration |\\\\n| Convex schema: `processHistoryItems` with correct fields and indexes | SATISFIED | Fields match tech-design spec exactly; both required indexes present |\\\\n| Convex schema: `processSideWorkItems` with correct fields and indexes | SATISFIED | Fields match spec; `by_processId_and_updatedAt` index present |\\\\n| Convex schema: `processOutputs` with correct fields and indexes | SATISFIED | Fields match spec; `by_processId_and_updatedAt` index present |\\\\n| `processes` table: `currentRequestHistoryItemId` pointer added | SATISFIED | Present in `processesTableFields`; typed as `v.union(v.id('processHistoryItems'), v.null())` |\\\\n| New Convex modules use guideline-compliant patterns | SATISFIED | New table modules (`processHistoryItems.ts`, `processSideWorkItems.ts`, `processOutputs.ts`) export only field definitions; no query/mutation functions yet; no debt introduced |\\\\n| **Modified Convex module `processes.ts` normalized to Epic 2 Convex guidelines** | **VIOLATED** | `queryGeneric`/`mutationGeneric`, `ctx: any`, unbounded `.collect()`, duplicate index — all present after modification; see Finding F-1 |\\\\n| Fixtures: history items — all 6 kinds, finalized/current variants | SATISFIED | `process-history.ts` covers all kinds; both lifecycle states represented |\\\\n| Fixtures: materials — artifact, linked output, standalone output, source, empty | SATISFIED | All required variants in `materials.ts` |\\\\n| Fixtures: side-work — running, completed, failed, empty, error | SATISFIED | `side-work.ts` covers all cases |\\\\n| Fixtures: process surface — ready, early (empty), degraded, unavailable, access-denied | SATISFIED | `process-surface.ts` covers all 5 cases |\\\\n| Fixtures: live process — snapshot, upsert, complete, error, cleared-request | SATISFIED | `live-process.ts` covers all message forms; builder helper present |\\\\n| `renderShell` test helper supports non-`/projects` bootstrap paths | SATISFIED | `render-shell.ts` now accepts arbitrary `pathname`/`search` overrides |\\\\n| No user-visible Story 1+ behavior introduced | SATISFIED | See note on bootstrap.ts below; the fall-through to shell loading is placeholder behavior, not process surface behavior |\\\\n| Story files can reference foundation without redefining vocabulary | SATISFIED | All vocabulary defined once; `index.ts` re-exports from all four contract files |\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## TEST_DIFF_AUDIT\\\\n\\\\n**Git diff result:** No test file changes between `c9a63ef` and HEAD.\\\\n\\\\n**Verification bundle claim:** \\\\\\\"Tests Added Or Updated: none. Story 0 is scaffolding-only. Chunk 0 specifies 0 TC tests and 0 non-TC tests.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n**Cross-check against test plan:** The test plan lists Story 0 (Chunk 0) explicitly as zero TC tests and zero non-TC tests, with `red-verify` (typecheck + build) as the exit gate. Claim is CONSISTENT with the test plan specification.\\\\n\\\\n**Assessment:** OBSERVED. No executable test coverage was expected or introduced. This is correct per the test plan.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## CONTRACT_AND_FIXTURE_FINDINGS\\\\n\\\\n**Contracts are internally consistent.** All four contract files (`schemas.ts`,\\\\n`process-work-surface.ts`, `live-process-updates.ts`, `state.ts`) import cleanly\\\\nfrom each other. `index.ts` re-exports all four. Router and store both import\\\\nfrom `index.ts` as expected.\\\\n\\\\n**Live update discriminated union is complete.** All five entity types have typed\\\\nschemas; the error variant restricts entity type to `history | materials |\\\\nside_work`. The `completedAt` and `correlationId` fields are nullable across all\\\\nvariants, consistent with the spec.\\\\n\\\\n**`currentRequestLiveDataMessageSchema` constrains `entityId` to literal\\\\n`'current_request'`.** This is tighter than the spec but correct for the single\\\\n`current_request` projection slot.\\\\n\\\\n**One fixture modeling concern (non-blocking):**\\\\n\\\\n`processLiveUnavailableErrorFixture` in `process-surface.ts` (lines 103–107):\\\\n\\\\n```ts\\\\nexport const processLiveUnavailableErrorFixture = requestErrorSchema.parse({\\\\n  code: 'PROCESS_LIVE_UPDATES_UNAVAILABLE',\\\\n  message: 'Live updates are currently unavailable.',\\\\n  status: 503,\\\\n});\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nThe design resolution (tech-design.md Issue table) explicitly states live\\\\nunavailability is NOT an HTTP bootstrap failure — it is a post-bootstrap live\\\\ntransport state expressed through `live.connectionState` and `live.error`. This\\\\nfixture is structurally valid (the `live.error` field in `ProcessSurfaceState`\\\\naccepts `requestErrorSchema`) but the `status: 503` field implies an HTTP\\\\nresponse code, which will never be returned for this case. Any Story 6\\\\nimplementer who follows this fixture as a template for handling live failures may\\\\nmodel the wrong client path. See Finding F-2.\\\\n\\\\n**Section error envelopes include `superRefine` consistency guard.** All three\\\\nenvelope types (`history`, `materials`, `sideWork`) enforce `error` presence\\\\nwhen `status === 'error'`. This is correct and forward-compatible.\\\\n\\\\n**`processSurfaceAvailableActionSchema` (work surface) vs `processAvailableActionSchema`\\\\n(shell):** The two schemas have different vocabularies (`start` vs `open`,\\\\n`rehydrate` absent in surface). This is intentional and correctly models the\\\\nEpic 1 shell vocabulary vs Epic 2 surface vocabulary. Not a defect.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## CONVEX_GUIDELINE_FINDINGS\\\\n\\\\n**Convex AI guidelines** (per `convex/_generated/ai/guidelines.md` referenced in\\\\nCLAUDE.md): typed query/mutation imports, proper ctx types, `withIndex` over\\\\n`filter`, bounded reads with `.take(n)`.\\\\n\\\\n**New table modules (`processHistoryItems.ts`, `processSideWorkItems.ts`,\\\\n`processOutputs.ts`):** Export field definitions only; no function\\\\nimplementations yet. No guideline violations introduced. Clean.\\\\n\\\\n**`convex/schema.ts`:** New tables `processHistoryItems`, `processSideWorkItems`,\\\\n`processOutputs` correctly defined with required indexes per the tech design\\\\nIndex Plan. One debt item present in the `processes` table declaration — see\\\\nFinding F-1.\\\\n\\\\n**`convex/processes.ts`:** MAJOR violation. See Finding F-1 for full detail.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## COMPLETENESS_GAPS\\\\n\\\\n1. **Process service skeletons absent:** `process-access.service.ts`,\\\\n   `process-start.service.ts`, `process-resume.service.ts`,\\\\n   `process-response.service.ts`, reader services, and summary builders are\\\\n   not present. The verification bundle does not list them; the tech-design\\\\n   Skeleton Requirements tables assign them to later stories (they appear in\\\\n   Flow 1–5 skeleton tables but Story 0 is foundation only). **Assessment:**\\\\n   ACCEPTABLE for Story 0. These are Story 1–3 deliverables.\\\\n\\\\n2. **`bootstrap.ts` `loadParsedRoute` falls through to project-shell loading for\\\\n   `process-work-surface` routes.** When the route kind is\\\\n   `process-work-surface`, the function calls `getProjectShell` as a\\\\n   placeholder. This is within scope (Story 0 does not own process bootstrap\\\\n   behavior), but Story 1 must add a dedicated `process-work-surface` branch\\\\n   and stop loading the project shell for that route. This is not a Story 0\\\\n   violation, but it is a known functional gap that Story 1 must close.\\\\n\\\\n3. **`connectedProcessSurfaceStateFixture` has `project: null`.** A connected\\\\n   live state that has already bootstrapped should normally have project info\\\\n   populated. The fixture is technically valid per schema but may require a\\\\n   richer variant for Story 6 tests. Minor fixture gap.\\\\n\\\\n4. **`process-module-registry.ts` interface deviates slightly from tech-design-server.md.**\\\\n   The design shows `buildSurfaceProjection` receiving `process: ProcessRecord`,\\\\n   but the implementation passes `processId: string` instead. This reduces the\\\\n   data available to process module implementations. Acceptable for Story 0\\\\n   scaffolding; Story 3/4 must confirm the signature is sufficient.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## BLOCKING_FINDINGS\\\\n\\\\n### F-1 — MAJOR | HIGH confidence\\\\n\\\\n**Finding:** `convex/processes.ts` was modified in Story 0 (added\\\\n`currentRequestHistoryItemId` to the field schema and to `createProcess`) but\\\\nwas not normalized to Epic 2 Convex guideline standards.\\\\n\\\\n**Evidence (OBSERVED):**\\\\n\\\\n```ts\\\\n// convex/processes.ts line 1\\\\nimport { mutationGeneric as mutation, queryGeneric as query } from 'convex/server';\\\\n\\\\n// line 37\\\\nhandler: async (ctx: any, args: any) => {\\\\n\\\\n// line 40\\\\n  .withIndex('by_projectId_updatedAt', ...)\\\\n  .order('desc')\\\\n  .collect();   // unbounded collect on processes table\\\\n\\\\n// convex/schema.ts lines 25–26 — duplicate index names for same fields\\\\n.index('by_projectId_updatedAt', ['projectId', 'updatedAt'])\\\\n.index('by_projectId_and_updatedAt', ['projectId', 'updatedAt']),\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n**Design requirement (OBSERVED):** tech-design.md Issue table, row 6:\\\\n\\\\n> \\\\\\\"The current Convex scaffold uses `queryGeneric`/`mutationGeneric`, `ctx:\\\\n> any`, and some broad `.collect()` reads that do not match the generated\\\\n> Convex AI guidelines... This design standardizes new and modified Convex\\\\n> modules on guideline-compliant validators, typed contexts, bounded queries,\\\\n> and explicit indexes. Existing scaffold shortcuts are treated as\\\\n> implementation debt, not as design precedent.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nThe verification bundle orchestrator note also explicitly flags this as a\\\\nscrutiny point.\\\\n\\\\n**Disproof attempt:** Could Story 0 defer normalization on the grounds that the\\\\nmodification was additive (schema field only) and the function bodies were not\\\\ntouched? Weak. The field definition change and the `createProcess` mutation body\\\\n(which now inserts `currentRequestHistoryItemId: null`) both touched the file.\\\\nThe design says modified modules adopt the new standard.\\\\n\\\\n**Impact:** `processes.ts` becomes the de-facto reference for later story\\\\nimplementers. If this file is not normalized, Stories 2–6 will add functions\\\\nusing `ctx: any`, `queryGeneric`, and unbounded `.collect()` patterns because\\\\nthey look like established precedent. The duplicate index is also functional\\\\ndebt — two indexes on identical columns consume unnecessary storage and may\\\\ncause confusion in query planning.\\\\n\\\\n**Validation step:** Normalize `convex/processes.ts`:\\\\n- Replace `queryGeneric as query` and `mutationGeneric as mutation` with typed\\\\n  imports from `convex/server`\\\\n- Replace `ctx: any` / `args: any` with proper `QueryCtx`/`MutationCtx` types\\\\n  and explicit argument validators\\\\n- Replace `.collect()` with `.take(n)` (bound appropriate to the list size)\\\\n- Remove the duplicate `by_projectId_updatedAt` index, keeping only\\\\n  `by_projectId_and_updatedAt`\\\\n- Re-run `typecheck && build`\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## NONBLOCKING_WARNINGS\\\\n\\\\n### F-2 — MINOR | MEDIUM confidence\\\\n\\\\n**Finding:** `processLiveUnavailableErrorFixture` models live unavailability as\\\\na `requestErrorSchema` row with `status: 503`.\\\\n\\\\n**Evidence:** `tests/fixtures/process-surface.ts` lines 103–107.\\\\n\\\\n**Design stance:** tech-design.md Q8 answer and resolved Issue 5 — live\\\\nunavailability is a post-bootstrap live transport state, not an HTTP error.\\\\n`PROCESS_LIVE_UPDATES_UNAVAILABLE` belongs to the `live.error` field of\\\\n`ProcessSurfaceState`, not to the top-level HTTP error response. The `status:\\\\n503` field in this fixture has no corresponding HTTP route that will ever return\\\\nit.\\\\n\\\\n**Impact:** Story 6 implementers may incorrectly model live reconnect failure\\\\nas an HTTP-layer response rather than a transport-layer state. The `live.error`\\\\nfield is typed as `requestErrorSchema.nullable()`, so the fixture type is\\\\nvalid; the mislead is semantic, not a compile-time failure.\\\\n\\\\n**Suggested fix:** Rename to `processLiveTransportErrorFixture` and clarify in\\\\na JSDoc comment that it represents a `live.error` payload, not an HTTP response.\\\\nRemove or zero out the `status` field, or document why 503 was chosen.\\\\n\\\\n### F-3 — MINOR | HIGH confidence\\\\n\\\\n**Finding:** Duplicate Convex index on `processes` table.\\\\n\\\\n**Evidence:** `convex/schema.ts` lines 25–26:\\\\n\\\\n```ts\\\\n.index('by_projectId_updatedAt', ['projectId', 'updatedAt'])\\\\n.index('by_projectId_and_updatedAt', ['projectId', 'updatedAt']),\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nBoth index the same two fields. The old name (`by_projectId_updatedAt`) is used\\\\nin `processes.ts` line 40. This is covered by F-1's normalization fix.\\\\n\\\\n### F-4 — MINOR | HIGH confidence\\\\n\\\\n**Finding:** `bootstrap.ts` falls through to project-shell loading for\\\\n`process-work-surface` routes. Story 1 must add a dedicated branch.\\\\n\\\\n**Evidence:** `apps/platform/client/app/bootstrap.ts` `loadParsedRoute()`\\\\nfunction, lines 155–234. Only `project-index` has an explicit branch; all other\\\\nroute kinds (including `process-work-surface`) fall through to `getProjectShell`.\\\\n\\\\n**Impact:** On a process route, the shell API is called unnecessarily. More\\\\ncritically, the process work surface data is never fetched until Story 1 adds\\\\nthe branch. Story 1 must not leave this fallthrough in place.\\\\n\\\\n**Story 0 scope verdict:** ACCEPTABLE for Story 0. Not a Story 0 violation.\\\\nFlagged so Story 1 does not inherit it silently.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## UNRESOLVED\\\\n\\\\n### U-1 — LOW confidence\\\\n\\\\n**Issue:** `process-module-registry.ts` `ProcessWorkSurfaceModule.buildSurfaceProjection`\\\\nreceives `processId: string` rather than `process: ProcessRecord` as specified\\\\nin tech-design-server.md.\\\\n\\\\n**Evidence INFERRED:** The tech design shows `process: ProcessRecord` in the\\\\ninterface. The implementation uses `processId: string`. The change reduces what\\\\nmodule implementations can access about the process record in one call.\\\\n\\\\n**Why unresolved:** Story 0 is scaffolding only; no process module\\\\nimplementations exist yet. It is possible this simplified signature was a\\\\ndeliberate Story 0 choice with the intent to expand later, or it is an\\\\nunintentional deviation. The impact cannot be confirmed until Stories 2–3\\\\nimplement the first real module.\\\\n\\\\n**Validation step:** When Story 2/3 authors the first concrete process module,\\\\nconfirm whether `processId` alone is sufficient for `buildSurfaceProjection` or\\\\nwhether `process: ProcessRecord` is needed.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## GATE_RESULT\\\\n\\\\n**Claimed:** `corepack pnpm run typecheck && corepack pnpm run build` → PASS (verification bundle).\\\\n\\\\n**Independently verified:** NO. The `typecheck` command required approval that\\\\nwas not granted during this review session. The gate result is ACCEPTED as\\\\nclaimed from the verification bundle. If the gate fails when run independently,\\\\nthe verdict escalates to BLOCK.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## What else I noticed but chose not to report\\\\n\\\\n- **`processAvailableActionSchema` in `schemas.ts` includes `open`, `rehydrate`** values\\\\n  that do not appear in the work-surface `processSurfaceAvailableActionSchema`. This is\\\\n  correct — they serve the Epic 1 shell context — but the coexistence of two\\\\n  overlapping action enums creates a long-term maintenance question about\\\\n  whether they eventually merge. I did not report this because it is a design\\\\n  future-risk, not a Story 0 defect.\\\\n\\\\n- **`deriveAvailableActions` in `processes.ts` returns `['open']` for draft status** while\\\\n  the Epic 2 contract returns `['start']` for draft. This is correct scope separation\\\\n  (the Convex function feeds the shell summary, not the work surface) but the divergence\\\\n  will widen as the work surface action vocabulary grows. Not reported because it is\\\\n  intentional for the current milestone.\\\\n\\\\n- **`app.ts` still has the health route returning `story: 'story-5-return-and-recovery-visibility'`**\\\\n  which is Epic 1's last story label. This label is stale after Story 0 was applied.\\\\n  A cosmetic artifact, not a functional issue.\\\\n\\\\n- **`processWorkSurfaceService` is declared but `processLiveHub` is NOT decorated on the\\\\n  Fastify instance** (it is passed to the websocket plugin but not decorated via\\\\n  `app.decorate('processLiveHub', ...)` at the app level). The plugin does the decoration\\\\n  inside its own scope. This means Fastify routes cannot access `app.processLiveHub`\\\\n  unless they are registered after the plugin. The TypeScript declaration `FastifyInstance.processLiveHub`\\\\n  is in `websocket.plugin.ts` and will be available after the plugin runs. This is\\\\n  correct sequencing, but the pattern differs from how other services are decorated.\\\\n  Not reported because it is architecturally sound.\\\\n\\\\n- **`connectedProcessSurfaceStateFixture` uses a `processId` from `waitingProcessSurfaceFixture`**\\\\n  but `processUpsertLiveFixture` uses `runningProcessSurfaceFixture.processId` (a different\\\\n  ID). The two fixtures are not pointing at the same process, so reconciliation tests\\\\n  that mix them would apply an upsert from a different process into the connected state.\\\\n  This may cause false negatives in reconciliation tests. I chose not to report it\\\\n  because no reconciliation tests exist yet in Story 0, and the fixture builder pattern\\\\n  (`buildLiveProcessMessageFixture`) provides a clean override path.\\\\n\\\"}},{\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Write\\\",\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_01U5Bjdag7nNrWUuSkwfyNnk\\\",\\\"tool_input\\\":{\\\"file_path\\\":\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/00-foundation/sonnet-review.md\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"# Story 0 Foundation — Compliance Review\\\\n\\\\n**Reviewer:** Claude Sonnet 4.6  \\\\n**Date:** 2026-04-14  \\\\n**Story base commit:** `c9a63ef2b71e7bdfa380a6c7313f3a2b38e7c9ac`  \\\\n**Verification bundle:** `story-verification/00-foundation/verification-bundle.md`\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## VERDICT: REVISE\\\\n\\\\nOne MAJOR finding (Convex normalization) must be resolved before the foundation\\\\nis clean enough to be the reference baseline for Stories 1–6. The issue is a\\\\nconfirmed scope omission, not speculative. Everything else is PASS or MINOR.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## STORY0_REQUIREMENTS_MATRIX\\\\n\\\\n| Requirement | Status | Notes |\\\\n|---|---|---|\\\\n| Shared route constant `/projects/{projectId}/processes/{processId}` | SATISFIED | `processWorkSurfaceRouteTemplate` and companion patterns defined in `process-work-surface.ts` |\\\\n| Shared endpoint vocabulary (bootstrap, start, resume, respond, live WS) | SATISFIED | All six path patterns defined and exported; path-builder helpers present |\\\\n| `process.processType` values | SATISFIED | `ProductDefinition`, `FeatureSpecification`, `FeatureImplementation` |\\\\n| `process.status` values | SATISFIED | All 7 values in `processStatusSchema` and mirrored in Convex validator |\\\\n| `process.availableActions` values (`start`, `respond`, `resume`, `review`, `restart`) | SATISFIED | `processSurfaceAvailableActionSchema` in `process-work-surface.ts` |\\\\n| `history.kind` values | SATISFIED | All 6 kinds in `processHistoryItemKindSchema` |\\\\n| `history.lifecycleState` values | SATISFIED | `current`, `finalized` |\\\\n| `live.messageType` values | SATISFIED | `snapshot`, `upsert`, `complete`, `error` |\\\\n| `live.entityType` values | SATISFIED | All 5 entity types |\\\\n| Shared section error contract (code, message) | SATISFIED | `processSurfaceSectionErrorSchema` with typed code enum |\\\\n| Shared live update contract (all 9 fields per spec) | SATISFIED | `liveProcessMessageBaseSchema` covers all fields; discriminated union covers all entity types |\\\\n| `processSurface` state slice in `AppState` | SATISFIED | `processSurfaceStateSchema` in `state.ts`; `processSurface` key in `appStateSchema`; default values in `defaultAppState` |\\\\n| Route parsing: process route matched before project-shell pattern | SATISFIED | `processMatch` check precedes `projectMatch` in `parseRoute()` |\\\\n| `processId` and `projectId` populated in `processSurface` slice on route parse | SATISFIED | `getProcessSurfaceRouteIdentity` called in `bootstrap.ts`; identity fields stored in `processSurface` initial state |\\\\n| Pure `applyLiveProcessMessage` helper | SATISFIED | Implemented in `process-live.ts`; handles all 5 entity types and error messages; stale-message guard present |\\\\n| WebSocket plugin scaffold in server | SATISFIED | `websocket.plugin.ts` registers with Fastify; decorates app with `NoopProcessLiveHub` |\\\\n| Process routes scaffold in server | SATISFIED | `routes/processes.ts` stubs `registerProcessRoutes`; exports route-pattern constants |\\\\n| `ProcessWorkSurfaceService` interface + NotImplemented stub | SATISFIED | `process-work-surface.service.ts`; stub throws `story0NotImplementedErrorCode` |\\\\n| `ProcessModuleRegistry` interface + functional registry | SATISFIED | Registry is functional (register/get/list); throws NotImplemented when no module registered |\\\\n| `ProcessLiveHub` interface + `NoopProcessLiveHub` | SATISFIED | In `process-live-hub.ts`; subscribe and publish both no-ops |\\\\n| `app.ts` registers websocket plugin and process routes in correct order | SATISFIED | `websocketPlugin` registered before `registerProcessRoutes`; `ProcessLiveHub` wired as optional decoration |\\\\n| Convex schema: `processHistoryItems` with correct fields and indexes | SATISFIED | Fields match tech-design spec exactly; both required indexes present |\\\\n| Convex schema: `processSideWorkItems` with correct fields and indexes | SATISFIED | Fields match spec; `by_processId_and_updatedAt` index present |\\\\n| Convex schema: `processOutputs` with correct fields and indexes | SATISFIED | Fields match spec; `by_processId_and_updatedAt` index present |\\\\n| `processes` table: `currentRequestHistoryItemId` pointer added | SATISFIED | Present in `processesTableFields`; typed as `v.union(v.id('processHistoryItems'), v.null())` |\\\\n| New Convex modules use guideline-compliant patterns | SATISFIED | New table modules export field definitions only; no function implementations yet; no debt introduced |\\\\n| **Modified Convex module `processes.ts` normalized to Epic 2 Convex guidelines** | **VIOLATED** | `queryGeneric`/`mutationGeneric`, `ctx: any`, unbounded `.collect()`, duplicate index — all present after modification; see Finding F-1 |\\\\n| Fixtures: history items — all 6 kinds, finalized/current variants | SATISFIED | `process-history.ts` covers all kinds; both lifecycle states represented |\\\\n| Fixtures: materials — artifact, linked output, standalone output, source, empty | SATISFIED | All required variants in `materials.ts` |\\\\n| Fixtures: side-work — running, completed, failed, empty, error | SATISFIED | `side-work.ts` covers all cases |\\\\n| Fixtures: process surface — ready, early (empty), degraded, unavailable, access-denied | SATISFIED | `process-surface.ts` covers all 5 cases |\\\\n| Fixtures: live process — snapshot, upsert, complete, error, cleared-request | SATISFIED | `live-process.ts` covers all message forms; builder helper present |\\\\n| `renderShell` test helper supports non-`/projects` bootstrap paths | SATISFIED | `render-shell.ts` accepts arbitrary `pathname`/`search` overrides |\\\\n| No user-visible Story 1+ behavior introduced | SATISFIED | Bootstrap falls through to shell loading as placeholder — not process surface behavior |\\\\n| Story files can reference foundation without redefining vocabulary | SATISFIED | All vocabulary defined once; `index.ts` re-exports from all four contract files |\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## TEST_DIFF_AUDIT\\\\n\\\\n**Git diff result:** No test file changes between `c9a63ef` and HEAD.\\\\n\\\\n**Verification bundle claim:** \\\\\\\"Tests Added Or Updated: none. Story 0 is\\\\nscaffolding-only. Chunk 0 specifies 0 TC tests and 0 non-TC tests.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n**Cross-check against test plan:** The test plan lists Story 0 (Chunk 0)\\\\nexplicitly as zero TC tests and zero non-TC tests, with `red-verify`\\\\n(typecheck + build) as the exit gate.\\\\n\\\\n**Assessment:** OBSERVED. No executable test coverage was expected or\\\\nintroduced. This is correct per the test plan.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## CONTRACT_AND_FIXTURE_FINDINGS\\\\n\\\\nContracts are internally consistent. All four contract files import cleanly\\\\nfrom each other. `index.ts` re-exports all four. Router and store both import\\\\nfrom `index.ts` as expected.\\\\n\\\\nLive update discriminated union is complete. All five entity types have typed\\\\nschemas; the error variant restricts entity type to `history | materials |\\\\nside_work`. `completedAt` and `correlationId` fields are nullable across all\\\\nvariants, consistent with the spec.\\\\n\\\\n`currentRequestLiveDataMessageSchema` constrains `entityId` to the literal\\\\n`'current_request'`. Tighter than the spec but correct.\\\\n\\\\n**One fixture modeling concern (non-blocking):**\\\\n\\\\n`processLiveUnavailableErrorFixture` in `tests/fixtures/process-surface.ts`\\\\nlines 103–107 models live unavailability as a `requestErrorSchema` row with\\\\n`status: 503`. The tech-design.md resolved Issue 5 explicitly: live\\\\nunavailability is a post-bootstrap transport state, not an HTTP failure. The\\\\nfixture is structurally valid (the `live.error` field accepts\\\\n`requestErrorSchema`), but the `status: 503` value implies an HTTP response\\\\ncode that will never be returned for this case. See Finding F-2.\\\\n\\\\nSection error envelopes include `superRefine` consistency guards enforcing\\\\n`error` presence when `status === 'error'`. Correct and forward-compatible.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## CONVEX_GUIDELINE_FINDINGS\\\\n\\\\nNew table modules (`processHistoryItems.ts`, `processSideWorkItems.ts`,\\\\n`processOutputs.ts`) export field definitions only. No function\\\\nimplementations yet. No guideline violations introduced. Clean.\\\\n\\\\n`convex/schema.ts` new tables correctly use guideline-compliant indexes.\\\\nOne debt item in the `processes` table — see Finding F-1.\\\\n\\\\n`convex/processes.ts`: MAJOR violation. See Finding F-1.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## COMPLETENESS_GAPS\\\\n\\\\n1. **Process service skeletons absent:** `process-access.service.ts`,\\\\n   `process-start.service.ts`, `process-resume.service.ts`,\\\\n   `process-response.service.ts`, reader services, and summary builders are\\\\n   not present. The tech-design Skeleton Requirements tables assign these to\\\\n   later stories. ACCEPTABLE for Story 0.\\\\n\\\\n2. **`bootstrap.ts` falls through to project-shell loading for\\\\n   `process-work-surface` routes.** `loadParsedRoute` has explicit handling\\\\n   only for `project-index`; all other route kinds call `getProjectShell`.\\\\n   Within Story 0 scope (process bootstrap is Story 1), but Story 1 must add\\\\n   a dedicated branch and stop loading the shell for process routes.\\\\n\\\\n3. **`connectedProcessSurfaceStateFixture` has `project: null`.** Technically\\\\n   valid; a richer variant may be needed for Story 6 reconciliation tests.\\\\n\\\\n4. **`ProcessWorkSurfaceModule.buildSurfaceProjection` passes `processId:\\\\n   string` instead of `process: ProcessRecord`** as shown in\\\\n   tech-design-server.md. See UNRESOLVED U-1.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## BLOCKING_FINDINGS\\\\n\\\\n### F-1 — MAJOR | HIGH confidence\\\\n\\\\n**Finding:** `convex/processes.ts` was modified in Story 0 but not normalized\\\\nto Epic 2 Convex guideline standards.\\\\n\\\\n**Evidence (OBSERVED):**\\\\n\\\\n```ts\\\\n// line 1 — guideline violation: use typed query/mutation, not generics\\\\nimport { mutationGeneric as mutation, queryGeneric as query } from 'convex/server';\\\\n\\\\n// line 37 — guideline violation: ctx: any, args: any\\\\nhandler: async (ctx: any, args: any) => {\\\\n\\\\n// line 40 — guideline violation: unbounded .collect() on processes table\\\\n  .withIndex('by_projectId_updatedAt', ...)\\\\n  .order('desc')\\\\n  .collect();\\\\n\\\\n// convex/schema.ts lines 25–26 — duplicate index: same fields, two names\\\\n.index('by_projectId_updatedAt', ['projectId', 'updatedAt'])\\\\n.index('by_projectId_and_updatedAt', ['projectId', 'updatedAt']),\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n**Design requirement (OBSERVED):** tech-design.md Issue table, row 6:\\\\n\\\\n> \\\\\\\"This design standardizes new and modified Convex modules on\\\\n> guideline-compliant validators, typed contexts, bounded queries, and\\\\n> explicit indexes. Existing scaffold shortcuts are treated as implementation\\\\n> debt, not as design precedent.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nThe verification bundle orchestrator note also explicitly flags this as a\\\\nscrutiny point for verifiers.\\\\n\\\\n**Disproof attempt:** Could Story 0 defer normalization because the change was\\\\nadditive (schema field only)? Weak. The `processesTableFields` change and the\\\\n`createProcess` mutation body both touch the file; the design's normalization\\\\nrequirement applies to modified modules regardless of change size.\\\\n\\\\n**Impact:** `processes.ts` becomes the de-facto reference for later story\\\\nimplementers. Stories 2–6 will mirror `ctx: any` and `.collect()` because\\\\nthey look like established precedent. The duplicate index also causes\\\\nunnecessary storage overhead and introduces ambiguity about which index name\\\\nto use in queries.\\\\n\\\\n**Required fix:**\\\\n- Replace `queryGeneric as query` / `mutationGeneric as mutation` with typed\\\\n  imports (`query`, `mutation`, or `internalQuery`/`internalMutation`)\\\\n- Replace `ctx: any` / `args: any` with proper typed context and explicit\\\\n  argument validators\\\\n- Replace `.collect()` with `.take(n)` bounded by a suitable limit\\\\n- Remove the duplicate `by_projectId_updatedAt` index, keeping only\\\\n  `by_projectId_and_updatedAt`\\\\n- Re-run `typecheck && build`\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## NONBLOCKING_WARNINGS\\\\n\\\\n### F-2 — MINOR | MEDIUM confidence\\\\n\\\\n**Finding:** `processLiveUnavailableErrorFixture` uses `status: 503` and is\\\\nnamed to suggest it is a top-level error response rather than a `live.error`\\\\npayload.\\\\n\\\\n**Evidence:** `tests/fixtures/process-surface.ts` lines 103–107.\\\\n\\\\n**Design stance:** tech-design.md Q8 — live unavailability is a transport\\\\nstate, not an HTTP error. The fixture is type-valid (it fits `live.error`),\\\\nbut the naming and 503 status code may mislead Story 6 implementers.\\\\n\\\\n**Suggested fix:** Rename to `processLiveTransportErrorFixture`; add a JSDoc\\\\ncomment clarifying this is the `live.error` payload shape, not an HTTP\\\\nresponse body. Evaluate whether the `status` field should be omitted or\\\\ndocumented explicitly.\\\\n\\\\n### F-3 — MINOR | HIGH confidence (covered by F-1 fix)\\\\n\\\\nDuplicate `processes` table indexes `by_projectId_updatedAt` and\\\\n`by_projectId_and_updatedAt` index the same `['projectId', 'updatedAt']`\\\\nfields. Resolved as part of the F-1 normalization.\\\\n\\\\n### F-4 — MINOR | HIGH confidence\\\\n\\\\n`bootstrap.ts` `loadParsedRoute` falls through to `getProjectShell` for\\\\n`process-work-surface` routes. Not a Story 0 violation; Story 1 must add a\\\\ndedicated branch.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## UNRESOLVED\\\\n\\\\n### U-1 — LOW confidence\\\\n\\\\n`ProcessWorkSurfaceModule.buildSurfaceProjection` in\\\\n`process-module-registry.ts` receives `processId: string` rather than\\\\n`process: ProcessRecord` as specified in tech-design-server.md. Impact cannot\\\\nbe confirmed until Stories 2–3 implement the first concrete process module.\\\\nConfirm then whether the simplified signature is sufficient or whether the\\\\nfull ProcessRecord is needed.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## GATE_RESULT\\\\n\\\\n**Claimed:** `corepack pnpm run typecheck && corepack pnpm run build` → PASS\\\\n(per verification bundle).\\\\n\\\\n**Independently verified:** NO — the `typecheck` command required approval\\\\nthat was not granted during this review session. Gate result is ACCEPTED as\\\\nclaimed. If the gate fails when run independently, the verdict escalates to\\\\nBLOCK.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## What else I noticed but chose not to report\\\\n\\\\n- **`processAvailableActionSchema` (schemas.ts) vs `processSurfaceAvailableActionSchema`\\\\n  (process-work-surface.ts) vocabulary divergence** — `open`/`rehydrate` vs\\\\n  `start`. Correct by design (shell vs work-surface contexts), but the two\\\\n  enums will need to be managed carefully as the action model evolves.\\\\n\\\\n- **`deriveAvailableActions` in `processes.ts` returns `['open']` for draft\\\\n  status** while the Epic 2 surface contract uses `['start']`. Correct scope\\\\n  separation today; the divergence will widen.\\\\n\\\\n- **`app.ts` health route still returns `story: 'story-5-return-and-recovery-visibility'`**\\\\n  — stale label from Epic 1's last story. Cosmetic artifact, not functional.\\\\n\\\\n- **`processLiveHub` is decorated by the websocket plugin, not by `app.ts`\\\\n  directly** (unlike other services). Architecturally sound given plugin\\\\n  sequencing, but the pattern inconsistency may surprise Story 6 authors\\\\n  looking for hub access in routes.\\\\n\\\\n- **`connectedProcessSurfaceStateFixture` and `processUpsertLiveFixture` use\\\\n  different process IDs** (`waiting` vs `running`). Mixing them in a\\\\n  reconciliation test would apply an upsert for a different process into the\\\\n  connected state. No reconciliation tests exist yet in Story 0 so no\\\\n  false-negatives are currently triggered, but the fixture family should be\\\\n  made self-consistent in Story 6.\\\\n\\\"}}],\\\"terminal_reason\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"fast_mode_state\\\":\\\"off\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"8b25cd86-ea60-4616-95cb-e621e95188ef\\\"}\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:163:- Full-fidelity canonical archive of process history at low-level entry grain\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:164:- Turn derivation and later chunk/view derivation over archived history\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:273:The platform also preserves a full-fidelity canonical archive of low-level\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:275:archive. Turns are derived groupings over archived entries. Chunks, summaries,\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:298:| M5 | Feature 5 | Broader source-attachment and canonical-source workflows work across aligned Convex-backed artifacts and GitHub-backed repos | Yes - can the platform manage source attachment lifecycle, provenance, freshness, and archive-facing source truth coherently? |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:635:and archive-facing records those flows depend on. Feature 3 already covers the\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:639:process lifecycle, along with the archive-facing canonical-source model that\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:648:and a later Feature 5 epic focuses on the full-fidelity canonical archive and\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:651:Epic 6, and later archive/derived-view work follows within Feature 5.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:667:- Full-fidelity process archive and derived turn/chunk views\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:718:archive/derived-view slice assigned to Epic 7.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:738:**AC-39:** The platform preserves a full-fidelity canonical archive of process\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:742:**AC-40:** The canonical archive stores the following finalized low-level entry\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:747:partial objects as canonical archive entries.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:749:**AC-42:** The platform can derive turns from archived entries and later produce\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:751:the full-fidelity archive.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:778:- The platform preserves a full-fidelity canonical archive of process history.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:779:  Turns are derived from archived entries. Chunks and summaries are later\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:839:  after the repository-focused source-management and archive work are in place.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-prd.md:888:- [ ] Full-fidelity archive requirements, finalized-entry rules, and\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/00-foundation.md:14:- **Key Constraint:** The review surface must stay process-aware and version-aware without turning into a generic document-management product, archive browser, or broader publication workflow in the same epic.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/codex-impl-log.md:188:- The highest-risk seam is state coherence across durable bootstrap, live current-object updates, and future archive compatibility.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/codex-impl-log.md:207:- Convex modeling adds `processHistoryItems`, `processSideWorkItems`, `processOutputs`, and a `currentRequestHistoryItemId` pointer on `processes`.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/00-foundation/verification-bundle.md:59:- `convex/processHistoryItems.ts`\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/00-foundation/verification-bundle.md:92:convex/processHistoryItems.ts\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/03-markdown-and-mermaid-review.md:14:- **Key Constraint:** The review surface must stay process-aware and version-aware without turning into a generic document-management product, archive browser, or broader publication workflow in the same epic.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/04--artifact-review-and-package-surface/stories/03-markdown-and-mermaid-review.md:34:- Global archive browsing or arbitrary rich-media review support\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/00-foundation/verification-bundle-round-2.md:59:- `convex/processHistoryItems.ts`\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/tech-design.md:83:archive work. If Epic 6 inherited the current artifact assumptions, it would\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/05--artifact-model-and-review-provenance-alignment/tech-design.md:554:| Historical process-to-artifact relation browser | AC-1, AC-5 | Epic 5 keeps bounded current refs and package contexts, not a full historical relation product surface | Later archive/provenance UI work |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:35:The platform also preserves a full-fidelity canonical archive of process\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:72:tools, artifacts, sources, archive, and review.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:171:| Full-fidelity archive entries are canonical while turns are derived | Context-management features can evolve without rewriting the archive |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:172:| Chunks summarize turns instead of replacing them | Derived views remain rebuildable from the archive |\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:285:**Choice:** The platform preserves a full-fidelity canonical archive of process\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:293:**Consequence:** The archive is append-oriented and durable. It is not the same\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:299:**Choice:** The canonical archive stores the following finalized low-level entry\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:314:differently without overfitting the archive to provider-specific wire shapes.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:323:to the canonical archive. Only finalized/completed entries are appended.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:326:the durable archive should remain queryable, stable, and semantically useful\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:335:**Choice:** `Turn` is the primary grouping derived from archived entries.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:340:strategies, so chunking should not be baked into the archive grain.\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:695:- canonical archive thinking\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:698:- archive vs derived-view separation\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:710:- the overall platform architecture; reuse the archive/projection ideas, not the\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:844:- [ ] Canonical archive entry taxonomy and finalized-entry rule are explicit\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/core-platform-arch.md:845:- [ ] Turns and later chunks are clearly derived over archived entries\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:10:  archiveEntrySchema,\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:11:  archivePageSchema,\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:12:  archiveTurnPageSchema,\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:147:  finalizationKey: string;\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:148:  sourceObjectId?: string | null;\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:321:  appendProcessHistoryItem(args: {\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:744:>('processHistoryItems:listProcessHistoryItems');\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:746:const appendProcessHistoryItemMutation = makeFunctionReference<\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:758:>('processHistoryItems:appendProcessHistoryItem');\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:764:>('archiveEntries:appendArchiveEntry');\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:774:>('archiveEntries:listArchiveEntries');\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:784:>('archiveTurns:upsertArchiveTurns');\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:794:>('archiveTurns:listArchiveTurns');\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:1419:  async appendProcessHistoryItem(args: {\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:1442:    return archiveEntrySchema.parse({\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:1443:      archiveEntryId: `${args.processId}:archive:0`,\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:1449:      finalizationKey: args.finalizationKey,\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:1450:      sourceObjectId: args.sourceObjectId ?? null,\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:1464:    return archivePageSchema.parse({\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:1477:    return archiveTurnPageSchema.parse({\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:1928:  async appendProcessHistoryItem(args: {\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:1937:    return this.client.mutation(appendProcessHistoryItemMutation, args, {\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:2283:  private readonly processHistoryItemsByProcessId = new Map<string, ProcessHistoryItem[]>();\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:2284:  private readonly archiveEntriesByProcessId = new Map<string, ArchiveEntry[]>();\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:2285:  private readonly archiveTurnsByProcessId = new Map<string, DerivedTurn[]>();\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:2334:      processHistoryItemsByProcessId?: Record<string, ProcessHistoryItem[]>;\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:2335:      archiveEntriesByProcessId?: Record<string, ArchiveEntry[]>;\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:2336:      archiveTurnsByProcessId?: Record<string, DerivedTurn[]>;\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:2394:    for (const [processId, items] of Object.entries(args.processHistoryItemsByProcessId ?? {})) {\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:2395:      this.processHistoryItemsByProcessId.set(processId, items);\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:2398:    for (const [processId, items] of Object.entries(args.archiveEntriesByProcessId ?? {})) {\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:2399:      this.archiveEntriesByProcessId.set(\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:2405:    for (const [processId, turns] of Object.entries(args.archiveTurnsByProcessId ?? {})) {\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:2406:      this.archiveTurnsByProcessId.set(\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3132:    return this.processHistoryItemsByProcessId.get(args.processId) ?? [];\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3135:  async appendProcessHistoryItem(args: {\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3144:    const existingHistory = this.processHistoryItemsByProcessId.get(args.processId) ?? [];\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3157:    this.processHistoryItemsByProcessId.set(args.processId, nextHistory);\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3163:    const existingEntries = this.archiveEntriesByProcessId.get(args.processId) ?? [];\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3165:      (entry) => entry.finalizationKey === args.finalizationKey,\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3173:    const nextEntry = archiveEntrySchema.parse({\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3174:      archiveEntryId: `${args.processId}:archive:${sequence + 1}`,\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3180:      finalizationKey: args.finalizationKey,\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3181:      sourceObjectId: args.sourceObjectId ?? null,\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3193:    this.archiveEntriesByProcessId.set(args.processId, [...existingEntries, nextEntry]);\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3203:    const entries = [...(this.archiveEntriesByProcessId.get(args.processId) ?? [])].sort(\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3213:    return archivePageSchema.parse({\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3225:    this.archiveTurnsByProcessId.set(\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3238:    const turns = [...(this.archiveTurnsByProcessId.get(args.processId) ?? [])].sort(\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3248:    return archiveTurnPageSchema.parse({\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3976:    const existingHistory = this.processHistoryItemsByProcessId.get(processId) ?? [];\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3982:    this.processHistoryItemsByProcessId.set(processId, nextHistory);\\n./apps/platform/server/services/projects/platform-store.ts:3995:    const existingHistory = this.processHistoryItemsByProcessId.get(processId) ?? [];\\n./docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/00-foundation/sonnet-review-round-2.json:1:{\\\"type\\\":\\\"result\\\",\\\"subtype\\\":\\\"success\\\",\\\"is_error\\\":false,\\\"duration_ms\\\":421071,\\\"duration_api_ms\\\":420567,\\\"num_turns\\\":45,\\\"result\\\":\\\"The write needs your approval. While you decide, here is the full review:\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## VERDICT: PASS\\\\n\\\\nBoth round-1 defects are genuinely closed. One bundle claim is materially inaccurate in its description (not in the code). No blocking findings.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## STORY 0 REQUIREMENTS MATRIX\\\\n\\\\n| Requirement | Status |\\\\n|---|---|\\\\n| Shared route and endpoint naming | SATISFIED |\\\\n| Shared process/action/history/live vocabulary | SATISFIED |\\\\n| Shared section error contract | SATISFIED |\\\\n| Shared live update contract | SATISFIED |\\\\n| Fixtures: ready/empty/error for all sections | SATISFIED |\\\\n| Fixtures: live-update messages across all entity types | SATISFIED |\\\\n| Test helper: bootstrap rendering | SATISFIED |\\\\n| Test helper: live-update application | SATISFIED |\\\\n| Test helper: reconnect reconciliation | PARTIALLY SATISFIED — state fixture + dedup logic exist; no exported reconciliation helper function |\\\\n| No user-visible Story 1+ behavior | SATISFIED |\\\\n| Shared vocabulary single-sourced | SATISFIED |\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## TEST DIFF AUDIT\\\\n\\\\nThe git diff glob returned empty (likely path expansion mismatch); the file was verified directly. `tests/service/client/process-live.test.ts` contains exactly two tests:\\\\n\\\\n1. **Rejects mismatched processId vs payload.processId** — schema-level `superRefine` throws with `/payload\\\\\\\\.processId/i`\\\\n2. **Ignores cross-process message in apply helper** — `applyLiveProcessMessage` returns the state reference unchanged\\\\n\\\\nBoth match bundle claims. Base commit did not contain this test file.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## CONVEX GUIDELINE FINDINGS\\\\n\\\\n**Round-1 fix #1 — normalization: CONFIRMED CLOSED.**\\\\n`git show c9a63ef:convex/processes.ts` line 1 reads `mutationGeneric as mutation, queryGeneric as query`. Current code imports from `./_generated/server.js`. All handlers use typed `ctx.db` with bounded `.take(200)`.\\\\n\\\\n**Round-1 fix #2 — \\\\\\\"duplicate index removed\\\\\\\": CLAIM INACCURATE.** **(MAJOR)**\\\\n\\\\nThe base commit had:\\\\n```\\\\n.index('by_projectId', ['projectId'])\\\\n.index('by_projectId_updatedAt', ['projectId', 'updatedAt'])\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nThe current code has:\\\\n```\\\\n.index('by_projectId', ['projectId'])\\\\n.index('by_projectId_and_updatedAt', ['projectId', 'updatedAt'])\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nWhat happened: the compound index was **renamed** (`by_projectId_updatedAt` → `by_projectId_and_updatedAt`). No index was removed. Both non-duplicate indexes remain. The bundle claim \\\\\\\"duplicate `processes` index removed\\\\\\\" is a documentation inaccuracy — not a correctness defect.\\\\n\\\\nThe `by_projectId` simple index appears unreferenced within `processes.ts` (the query uses the compound index). Worth grepping across all convex files before Story 1.\\\\n\\\\n**Round-1 fix #3 — cross-process live upsert hole: CONFIRMED CLOSED.**\\\\n`processLiveDataMessageSchema` has a `superRefine` checking `value.payload.processId !== value.processId`. `applyLiveProcessMessage` guards `args.state.processId !== args.message.processId`. Both layers present. Test 1 exercises the schema guard; Test 2 exercises the reducer guard.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## CONTRACT AND FIXTURE FINDINGS\\\\n\\\\n**MINOR:** `z.union` used instead of `z.discriminatedUnion` for `liveProcessUpdateMessageSchema` — functionally correct, but produces less targeted parse errors.\\\\n\\\\n**MINOR:** `completedAt` is nullable at schema level for all message types including `complete` — no enforcement that complete messages carry a timestamp.\\\\n\\\\n**MINOR:** `processSurfaceAvailableActionSchema` intentionally excludes `'open'` and `'rehydrate'` that exist in the shell enum. Valid design, but later story authors need to know which enum applies.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## BLOCKING FINDINGS\\\\n\\\\nNone.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## NONBLOCKING WARNINGS\\\\n\\\\n1. **Bundle claim \\\\\\\"duplicate `processes` index removed\\\\\\\" is inaccurate.** Rename happened; nothing removed.\\\\n2. **`by_projectId` index may be dead.** Grep before Story 1; remove if unreferenced.\\\\n3. **`websocketPlugin` does not register `@fastify/websocket`** — intentional Story 0 scaffolding, but Story 2/3 implementers must add the actual registration.\\\\n4. **`bootstrap.ts` still calls `getProjectShell` for `process-work-surface` routes** — Story 1 must address or tolerate this.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## GATE RESULT\\\\n\\\\nApproval required to run shell commands. Bundle claims both typecheck and build passed. Schema coherence is confirmed structurally by file reads (all types align, all schemas parse in fixture constructors). No typecheck errors visible in code.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## Noticed but not reported\\\\n\\\\n- `isStaleMessage` treats messages from a different `subscriptionId` as **not stale** (returns `false` when IDs differ). Semantically this means old-subscription messages pass through — a potential reconnect-coherence gap in Story 2+.\\\\n- `processUpsertLiveFixture` uses a different process ID than `connectedProcessSurfaceStateFixture` without the naming making this obvious. Later test authors could be confused.\\\\n- Health endpoint label `'story-5-return-and-recovery-visibility'` is stale — not Story 0's code to change, but misleading.\\\",\\\"stop_reason\\\":\\\"end_turn\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"3b64d224-e648-4c11-9534-cfdf540431d0\\\",\\\"total_cost_usd\\\":1.0675963499999999,\\\"usage\\\":{\\\"input_tokens\\\":210,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":83943,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":1422967,\\\"output_tokens\\\":21686,\\\"server_tool_use\\\":{\\\"web_search_requests\\\":0,\\\"web_fetch_requests\\\":0},\\\"service_tier\\\":\\\"standard\\\",\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":83943,\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0},\\\"inference_geo\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"iterations\\\":[{\\\"input_tokens\\\":8,\\\"output_tokens\\\":1367,\\\"cache_read_input_tokens\\\":90851,\\\"cache_creation_input_tokens\\\":5501,\\\"cache_creation\\\":{\\\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\\\":0,\\\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\\\":5501},\\\"type\\\":\\\"message\\\"}],\\\"speed\\\":\\\"standard\\\"},\\\"modelUsage\\\":{\\\"claude-sonnet-4-6\\\":{\\\"inputTokens\\\":210,\\\"outputTokens\\\":21686,\\\"cacheReadInputTokens\\\":1422967,\\\"cacheCreationInputTokens\\\":83943,\\\"webSearchRequests\\\":0,\\\"costUSD\\\":1.0675963499999999,\\\"contextWindow\\\":200000,\\\"maxOutputTokens\\\":32000}},\\\"permission_denials\\\":[{\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Bash\\\",\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_01Hombj7z7xmf1CWdgP3u5za\\\",\\\"tool_input\\\":{\\\"command\\\":\\\"corepack pnpm run typecheck 2>&1 | tail -20\\\",\\\"timeout\\\":120000,\\\"description\\\":\\\"Run typecheck gate\\\"}},{\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Bash\\\",\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_01DQ5a8Mi6d5kWE8f74j7TzB\\\",\\\"tool_input\\\":{\\\"command\\\":\\\"corepack pnpm run typecheck\\\",\\\"timeout\\\":120000,\\\"description\\\":\\\"Run typecheck acceptance gate\\\"}},{\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Write\\\",\\\"tool_use_id\\\":\\\"toolu_017ujYpSg7T9fbPMgb6NyBbC\\\",\\\"tool_input\\\":{\\\"file_path\\\":\\\"/Users/leemoore/code/liminal-build/docs/spec-build/v2/epics/02--process-work-surface/story-verification/00-foundation/sonnet-review-round-2.md\\\",\\\"content\\\":\\\"# Sonnet Review: Story 0 Foundation Round 2\\\\n\\\\n- **Reviewer model:** claude-sonnet-4-6\\\\n- **Review date:** 2026-04-14\\\\n- **Story base commit:** `c9a63ef2b71e7bdfa380a6c7313f3a2b38e7c9ac`\\\\n- **Bundle reviewed:** `story-verification/00-foundation/verification-bundle-round-2.md`\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## VERDICT: PASS\\\\n\\\\nOne bundle claim is materially inaccurate (documented below as MAJOR). No claim misrepresents the correctness of the code itself — the inaccuracy is in the description of what changed, not in whether the round-1 hole is closed. The implementation is functionally sound, within Story 0 boundaries, and ready for Story 1 build.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## STORY 0 REQUIREMENTS MATRIX\\\\n\\\\n| Requirement | Status | Evidence |\\\\n|---|---|---|\\\\n| Shared route and endpoint naming for the process work surface | SATISFIED | `process-work-surface.ts` exports all six URL patterns and four path builders; `router.ts` correctly orders process-route match before project-shell match |\\\\n| Shared process status, action, history-item, and live-update vocabulary | SATISFIED | `processStatusSchema`, `processSurfaceAvailableActionSchema`, `processHistoryItemKindSchema`, `processHistoryItemLifecycleSchema`, `liveProcessMessageTypeSchema`, `liveProcessEntityTypeSchema` all defined in shared contracts; vocabulary matches Story 0 spec table exactly |\\\\n| Shared section error contract | SATISFIED | `processSurfaceSectionErrorSchema` with typed `code` enum (`PROCESS_SURFACE_HISTORY_LOAD_FAILED`, etc.) and non-empty `message` |\\\\n| Shared live update contract | SATISFIED | `liveProcessMessageBaseSchema` covers all nine required fields; entity-specific discriminated schemas enforce payload typing per entity type |\\\\n| Reusable fixtures covering ready, empty, and error section envelopes | SATISFIED | `process-history.ts`, `materials.ts`, `side-work.ts` each export all three section states; confirmed via schema parse validation in fixture file |\\\\n| Reusable fixtures for live-update messages | SATISFIED | `live-process.ts` exports fixtures for all five entity types (`process`, `history`, `current_request`, `materials`, `side_work`) across all message types; state fixtures for connected and reconnecting states |\\\\n| Test helpers: bootstrap rendering | SATISFIED | `render-shell.ts` supports arbitrary pathname overrides including process-surface routes; `bootstrap.ts` seeds `processSurface.projectId` and `processSurface.processId` from route parse |\\\\n| Test helpers: live-update application | SATISFIED | `process-live.ts` exports `applyLiveProcessMessage` covering all entity branches and stale-message guard |\\\\n| Test helpers: reconnect reconciliation scenarios | PARTIALLY SATISFIED | `reconnectingProcessSurfaceStateFixture` in `live-process.ts` and `mergeHistoryItems` deduplication in the apply helper exist; no explicit reconciliation helper function exported for later stories to call directly |\\\\n| Story 0 introduces no user-visible behavior conflicting with Stories 1–6 | SATISFIED | `registerProcessRoutes` is a no-op; `NotImplementedProcessWorkSurfaceService` throws 501; `NoopProcessLiveHub` does nothing; `ProcessModuleRegistry` initialises empty |\\\\n| Story files and coverage artifacts can reference foundation without redefining shared vocabulary | SATISFIED | `index.ts` re-exports all four contract modules; vocabulary is single-sourced |\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## TEST DIFF AUDIT\\\\n\\\\n**Confirmed by direct file read.** `tests/service/client/process-live.test.ts` contains exactly two tests:\\\\n\\\\n1. `rejects process messages whose top-level process id differs from the payload process id` — calls `liveProcessUpdateMessageSchema.parse()` with mismatched `processId`/`payload.processId`; expects throw matching `/payload\\\\\\\\.processId/i`. Matches bundle claim #1.\\\\n\\\\n2. `ignores process messages for another process surface` — constructs a valid cross-process message, applies it via `applyLiveProcessMessage` to `connectedProcessSurfaceStateFixture` (different `processId`), asserts referential identity (`toBe`). Matches bundle claim #2.\\\\n\\\\n**Git diff note:** The shell command `git diff c9a63ef -- \\\\\\\"*.test.*\\\\\\\"` returned empty. Most likely cause: the glob did not expand to include the test file path (globbing semantics in git differ from shell). The test file was verified directly via file read; its content is consistent with the bundle's \\\\\\\"Changed Test Files\\\\\\\" and \\\\\\\"Tests Added Or Updated\\\\\\\" sections.\\\\n\\\\n**Test count from base commit:** The base commit did not contain `tests/service/client/process-live.test.ts` (confirmed: it appears in `git status` as untracked relative to the working tree starting from `c9a63ef`). Round 2 added two new tests. No existing tests were deleted or modified.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## CONTRACT AND FIXTURE FINDINGS\\\\n\\\\n### F1 — `processSurfaceSummarySchema` uses a narrower action enum than `processSummarySchema`\\\\n\\\\n- **Finding:** `processSurfaceAvailableActionSchema` = `['start', 'respond', 'resume', 'review', 'restart']`. The Epic 1 shell uses `processAvailableActionSchema` = `['open', 'respond', 'resume', 'review', 'rehydrate', 'restart']`. The two schemas are intentionally separate — the shell uses `open` and `rehydrate`; the surface does not. Story 0 spec table lists exactly `start, respond, resume, review, restart`.\\\\n- **Severity:** MINOR\\\\n- **Confidence:** HIGH\\\\n- **Evidence:** `schemas.ts:23–31` and `process-work-surface.ts:55–62`\\\\n- **Disproof attempt:** Maybe the two enums should merge. They don't — `open` is a shell-level navigation action, not a surface-level action. The design distinction is valid.\\\\n- **Impact:** None now; later stories must be aware they draw from `processSurfaceAvailableActionSchema`, not from the shell enum.\\\\n- **Validation step:** Confirm Story 1+ fixtures use `processSurfaceAvailableActionSchema` actions only.\\\\n\\\\n### F2 — `liveProcessUpdateMessageSchema` uses `z.union` rather than `z.discriminatedUnion`\\\\n\\\\n- **Finding:** The six branches are combined via `z.union(...)`. Because `entityType` + `messageType` together fully discriminate every branch, a `z.discriminatedUnion` on `entityType` (with a nested union for the error case) would be marginally more efficient and produce clearer parse errors.\\\\n- **Severity:** MINOR\\\\n- **Confidence:** HIGH\\\\n- **Evidence:** `live-process-updates.ts:89–97`\\\\n- **Disproof attempt:** `z.union` is functionally correct and all union members are properly ordered (error message last). Parse errors may be less targeted, but Story 0 tests confirm correct acceptance/rejection behavior.\\\\n- **Impact:** Slightly noisier parse errors in future debugging. No correctness impact.\\\\n- **Validation step:** Future story review may want to migrate to discriminated union for parse-error quality, but not a Story 0 blocker.\\\\n\\\\n### F3 — `completedAt` nullable for all message types including `complete`\\\\n\\\\n- **Finding:** `liveProcessMessageBaseSchema` defines `completedAt: z.string().min(1).nullable()`. A `complete` message can therefore parse successfully with `completedAt: null`. The Story 0 spec says `completedAt` should be \\\\\\\"ISO 8601 UTC when present\\\\\\\". There is no schema-level enforcement that `complete` messages must carry a non-null `completedAt`.\\\\n- **Severity:** MINOR\\\\n- **Confidence:** HIGH\\\\n- **Evidence:** `live-process-updates.ts:32`, `live-process.ts:67–77` (fixture sets `completedAt` in `historyCompleteLiveFixture` and `currentRequestClearedLiveFixture`, so the pattern is demonstrated but not enforced)\\\\n- **Disproof attempt:** The tech design describes `completedAt` as \\\\\\\"when present\\\\\\\" — an optional field that signals completion timing but is not required. Story 0 fixtures correctly set it on complete messages. Schema enforcement is Story 1+ territory.\\\\n- **Impact:** Consumers of `complete` messages must null-check `completedAt` themselves.\\\\n- **Validation step:** Acceptable at Story 0 level.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## CONVEX GUIDELINE FINDINGS\\\\n\\\\n### F4 — `queryGeneric`/`mutationGeneric` imports removed; typed imports confirmed\\\\n\\\\n- **Finding:** Base commit `convex/processes.ts` imported `mutationGeneric as mutation` and `queryGeneric as query` from `'convex/server'`. Current code imports `mutation` and `query` from `'./_generated/server.js'`. All handlers now use typed `ctx.db` with proper Convex return types.\\\\n- **Severity:** N/A (fix confirmed)\\\\n- **Confidence:** HIGH\\\\n- **Evidence:** `git show c9a63ef:convex/processes.ts` (line 1 shows `mutationGeneric`); current `processes.ts:4` shows `from './_generated/server.js'`\\\\n- **Disproof attempt:** None — the before/after is deterministically visible in git.\\\\n- **Impact:** Round-1 finding confirmed closed.\\\\n\\\\n### F5 — `currentRequestHistoryItemId` field added to `processesTableFields`\\\\n\\\\n- **Finding:** Base commit `processesTableFields` did not include `currentRequestHistoryItemId`. Current code adds `currentRequestHistoryItemId: v.union(v.id('processHistoryItems'), v.null())`. This is correctly typed as a Convex ID reference, not a raw string. The `createProcess` mutation initialises it to `null`.\\\\n- **Severity:** N/A (correct addition)\\\\n- **Confidence:** HIGH\\\\n- **Evidence:** `processes.ts:29`, `processes.ts:65`\\\\n- **Impact:** Story 2 (current request projection) can locate the pinned request via this pointer.\\\\n\\\\n### F6 — `processes` table retains `by_projectId` index alongside `by_projectId_and_updatedAt`\\\\n\\\\n- **Finding:** Current schema has two indexes on `processes`: `by_projectId` (`['projectId']`) and `by_projectId_and_updatedAt` (`['projectId', 'updatedAt']`). The base commit also had two indexes, with the compound one named `by_projectId_updatedAt`. The only change was a **rename** of the compound index (`by_projectId_updatedAt` → `by_projectId_and_updatedAt`). **No index was removed.** The bundle claims \\\\\\\"duplicate `processes` index removed\\\\\\\" — this is inaccurate.\\\\n- **Severity:** MAJOR (bundle claim inaccuracy, not a code defect)\\\\n- **Confidence:** HIGH\\\\n- **Evidence:** `git show c9a63ef:convex/schema.ts` shows both `by_projectId` and `by_projectId_updatedAt` indexes; current `schema.ts:23–25` shows `by_projectId` and `by_projectId_and_updatedAt`\\\\n- **Disproof attempt:** Maybe the rename was an intentional partial fix and the full \\\\\\\"remove the redundant simple index\\\\\\\" fix is deferred. The code is functionally correct — `listProjectProcessSummaries` uses the compound index, and `by_projectId` is not used within `processes.ts`. Whether `by_projectId` is used by other Convex functions is not confirmed.\\\\n- **Impact:** The `by_projectId` index may be redundant. In Convex, compound indexes can serve single-field equality queries if the compound index's first field matches, so `by_projectId_and_updatedAt` would suffice for both the sorted list and any future by-projectId-only query. Retaining `by_projectId` has negligible runtime cost but is misleading.\\\\n- **Validation step:** Grep for `.withIndex('by_projectId', ...)` across all convex files to confirm whether the simple index is actually referenced. If unreferenced, remove it before or during Story 1.\\\\n\\\\n### F7 — `projectId as Id<'projects'>` type cast in `createProcess`\\\\n\\\\n- **Finding:** `processes.ts:70`: `const projectId = args.projectId as Id<'projects'>;` casts a validated `v.string()` argument to a Convex ID type. This is the existing repo pattern for string-typed foreign keys. The bundle acknowledges this as a residual risk.\\\\n- **Severity:** MINOR (acknowledged residual, within scope claim)\\\\n- **Confidence:** HIGH\\\\n- **Evidence:** `processes.ts:70`\\\\n- **Disproof attempt:** The `processes` table stores `projectId: v.string()`, so this field is genuinely a string at runtime. The cast is necessary to call `ctx.db.patch(projectId, ...)` on the `projects` table. The Convex guidelines prefer `v.id('projects')` for strong-typed foreign keys, but migrating this is out of Story 0 scope.\\\\n- **Impact:** No runtime error; minor type-safety gap.\\\\n- **Validation step:** Track as tech debt. Future story or migration will align to `v.id()` types.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## COMPLETENESS GAPS\\\\n\\\\n### G1 — `websocketPlugin` does not register `@fastify/websocket`\\\\n\\\\n- **Finding:** The plugin (`websocket.plugin.ts`) only decorates the Fastify instance with a `NoopProcessLiveHub`. It does not call `app.register(websocket, ...)` from `@fastify/websocket`. The tech design specifies that the plugin registers `@fastify/websocket`. This is intentional for Story 0 (scaffolding only), but a future story implementing live connections will need to add this registration step.\\\\n- **Severity:** MINOR (Story 0 scope is scaffold-only)\\\\n- **Confidence:** HIGH\\\\n- **Evidence:** `websocket.plugin.ts` (full file); tech-design-server.md describes \\\\\\\"Register websocket support\\\\\\\"\\\\n- **Impact:** None for Story 0. Story 2 or 3 (live updates) will need to extend this plugin.\\\\n\\\\n### G2 — `processLiveHub` decoration gap in `app.ts`\\\\n\\\\n- **Finding:** `app.ts:87`: `const processLiveHub = options.processLiveHub;` — this value may be `undefined`. The `websocketPlugin` is then registered with `{ processLiveHub }` which becomes `{ processLiveHub: undefined }`. The plugin handles `undefined` by falling back to `NoopProcessLiveHub`. However, the Fastify `FastifyInstance.processLiveHub` declaration in `websocket.plugin.ts` is added via plugin, but `app.ts` also declares `processLiveHub` in the `declare module 'fastify'` block on `process-live-hub.ts` — wait, no: `websocket.plugin.ts` owns the Fastify module augmentation for `processLiveHub`. The `declare module 'fastify'` in `app.ts` does NOT include `processLiveHub` — it only includes the project and process service decorations. So the only augmentation is from the plugin, which is correct.\\\\n- **Severity:** MINOR\\\\n- **Confidence:** MEDIUM\\\\n- **Evidence:** `app.ts:51–61` (no `processLiveHub` in declare block); `websocket.plugin.ts:8–12` (declares it there)\\\\n- **Impact:** No runtime impact. Correct separation — the hub is a plugin-owned decoration, not a service-owned one.\\\\n- **Validation step:** None required.\\\\n\\\\n### G3 — `bootstrap.ts` loads project shell for `process-work-surface` routes\\\\n\\\\n- **Finding:** `bootstrapApp`'s `loadParsedRoute` function falls into the shell-loading `else` branch for any non-`project-index` route, including `process-work-surface`. This means navigating to a process surface still calls `getProjectShell`. This is existing Epic 1 behavior; Story 0 extends the bootstrap only to seed `processSurface.projectId` and `processSurface.processId` from the route. The shell-loading side effect is not a Story 0 defect.\\\\n- **Severity:** MINOR (future story concern)\\\\n- **Confidence:** HIGH\\\\n- **Evidence:** `bootstrap.ts:151–234`\\\\n- **Impact:** Story 1 (process surface page) will need to either extend `loadParsedRoute` for `process-work-surface` or tolerate the shell loading alongside surface loading.\\\\n- **Validation step:** Story 1 implementation review should address this.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## BLOCKING FINDINGS\\\\n\\\\nNone.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## NONBLOCKING WARNINGS\\\\n\\\\n1. **Bundle claim \\\\\\\"duplicate `processes` index removed\\\\\\\" is inaccurate** (F6). The compound index was renamed, not removed; both indexes remain. Correct the bundle description if it feeds downstream records. No code change required.\\\\n\\\\n2. **`by_projectId` index on `processes` may be unreferenced** (F6 follow-on). Grep for usage before Story 1 and remove if dead.\\\\n\\\\n3. **`bootstrap.ts` health endpoint label is stale** (`app.ts:128`: `story: 'story-5-return-and-recovery-visibility'`). This is existing Epic 1 code not owned by Story 0, but it will mislead future ops debugging.\\\\n\\\\n4. **Reconnect reconciliation test helper is implicit, not exported** (G1 in requirements matrix). `mergeHistoryItems` and `reconnectingProcessSurfaceStateFixture` exist, but no exported `reconcileProcessSurfaceAfterReconnect` helper. Later stories may need to write their own reconciliation assertions. Low risk.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## UNRESOLVED\\\\n\\\\n| Item | Why Unresolved | Suggested Step |\\\\n|---|---|---|\\\\n| Gate result (typecheck + build) | Commands require shell approval; could not run independently | Bundle claims PASS; cross-check by running `corepack pnpm run typecheck && corepack pnpm run build` in clean shell |\\\\n| Whether `by_projectId` index is live in any other Convex file | grep not run | `grep -r 'by_projectId' convex/` — if no hits, safely remove |\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## GATE RESULT\\\\n\\\\n**UNVERIFIED (approval required to run).** Bundle claims both `corepack pnpm run typecheck` and `corepack pnpm run build` passed. All contract schema parse calls in fixtures are runtime validation — if typecheck passed, schema/type coherence across shared contracts, Convex table fields, and service interfaces is confirmed by the TypeScript compiler. There are no obvious type errors visible from file reads.\\\\n\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n## After the review: what I noticed but chose not to report\\\\n\\\\n- The `processWorkSurfaceRouteTemplate` constant uses `{projectId}/{processId}` brace style (non-Express). This is declared as `as const` and appears to be a display-only template, not used for routing. The actual routing pattern uses the `:param` style. No issue.\\\\n- The `applyLiveProcessMessage` function has a subtle asymmetry: it updates `live.subscriptionId` and `live.lastSequenceNumber` unconditionally on every processed message, even `error` messages. This means an error message can advance the sequence number, which prevents reprocessing a later remediation message with a lower sequence number if the subscription restarts. This is a Story 2 concern, not Story 0.\\\\n- `processUpsertLiveFixture` in `live-process.ts` uses `runningProcessSurfaceFixture.processId` (a different process than the `connectedProcessSurfaceStateFixture`). The fixture name does not signal \\\\\\\"cross-process\\\\\\\". A later story test author could be confused. The `buildLiveProcessMessageFixture` helper silently normalises `entityId` from the payload for `process` entity types, which masks this. Not a defect, but naming could be clearer.\\\\n- The `isStaleMessage` guard has an inverted staleness check — it returns `false` (not stale) when `state.live.subscriptionId !== message.subscriptionId`. This means messages from a different subscription are NOT treated as stale and will be applied. A message from an old subscription with a higher sequence number would pass through. The intent may be that subscription changes reset stale tracking. This is potentially a reconnect-coherence gap, but Story 0 does not own reconnect behaviour end-to-end.\\\\n\\\"}}],\\\"terminal_reason\\\":\\\"completed\\\",\\\"fast_mode_state\\\":\\\"off\\\",\\\"uuid\\\":\\\"c5e46e6e-09c2-483f-8c9c-6376381fb014\\\"}\\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/local-provider-adapter.ts:347:    processHistoryItems: [\\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/local-provider-adapter.ts:388:    'processHistoryItems',\\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/environment/local-provider-adapter.ts:420:      processHistoryItems: obj.processHistoryItems as ExecutionResult['processHistoryItems'],\\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/history-section.reader.ts:3:  processHistorySectionEnvelopeSchema,\\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/history-section.reader.ts:18:    return processHistorySectionEnvelopeSchema.parse({\\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-work-surface.service.ts:22:  processHistorySectionEnvelopeSchema,\\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-work-surface.service.ts:446:      return processHistorySectionEnvelopeSchema.parse({\\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:10:import { ArchiveFinalizationService } from '../archive/archive-finalization.service.js';\\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:11:import { buildAcceptedUserResponseArchiveFinalizationKey } from '../archive/process-history-compat.service.js';\\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:23:    private readonly archiveFinalizationService: Pick<\\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:53:      await this.archiveAcceptedUserResponse({\\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:89:      await this.archiveAcceptedUserResponse({\\n./apps/platform/server/services/processes/process-response.service.ts:140:  private async archiveAccep