 history before Epic 5 delivers the full canonical archive?\\\\n261:### Q8. What exact error and retry model should the work surface use when the durable bootstrap succeeds but live transport is unavailable?\\\\n276:Section-level failures inside `history`, `materials`, or `sideWork` follow the\\\\n280:## System View\\\\n282:### Top-Tier Surfaces Touched by Epic 2\\\\n288:| Artifacts | Inherited from platform tech arch | Supplies current artifact context for the materials section |\\\\n289:| Sources | Inherited from platform tech arch | Supplies current source context for the materials section |\\\\n291:| Review Workspace | Inherited from platform tech arch | Adjacent surface only; Epic 2 keeps current materials visible without delivering rich review workflows |\\\\n293:### System Context Diagram\\\\n306:        ProcessUI[Process Work Surface]\\\\n329:### External Contracts\\\\n331:#### Browser Entry Contracts\\\\n339:#### API and Live Contracts Used by Epic 2\\\\n349:#### Request-Level Error Contracts\\\\n360:#### Live Transport Status Codes\\\\n366:#### Section-Level Process Surface Error Contracts\\\\n371:| `materials` | `PROCESS_SURFACE_MATERIALS_LOAD_FAILED` | Current materials could not be read | Render materials section error state; keep process surface usable |\\\\n374:#### Runtime Prerequisites\\\\n384:## Repo Shape and Module Architecture Overview\\\\n386:### Repo Layout\\\\n410:│       │           ├── process-materials-section.ts # NEW\\\\n435:│       │           │   ├── materials-section.reader.ts # NEW\\\\n440:│       │               ├── process-materials.builder.ts # NEW\\\\n466:### Module Responsibility Matrix\\\\n478:| `apps/platform/server/services/processes/readers/*.ts` | NEW | Read bounded visible history, materials, and side-work sections from durable state | Convex queries, summary builders | AC-1.4, AC-4.x, AC-5.x, AC-6.6 |\\\\n490:### Dependency Map\\\\n536:## Shared Contract Interfaces\\\\n546:### Process Surface Types\\\\n609:  revisionLabel